# shared automation (symlink to canonical; per-project data stays in ./automation_data)
teamz-company-automation

# data/ is nightly churn (content-queue, nightly-status, course-task) and stays out of git.
# The exceptions below are NOT churn and must survive a lost laptop:
#   - course-radar-seeds.json : the strategy input for every future course
#   - course-ledger.json      : which pilots exist. Lost ledger = radar recreates duplicates.
#                               nightly-course-prompt.md also runs `git add data/course-ledger.json`,
#                               and git aborts the WHOLE add on an ignored path — so while this was
#                               ignored the course agent could never commit a pilot at all.
#   - manual-pull/            : owner-facing batch instructions, and the pulled Planner volumes,
#                               which cost a manual 15-minute export each to recreate.
# Note: `data/*` not `data/` — git cannot re-include a file whose parent dir is excluded.
data/*
!data/course-radar-seeds.json
!data/course-ledger.json
!data/noindex-courses.json
# Measured SERP composition — each keyword cost a Firecrawl credit, and the cached raw results are
# what let the authority model be recomputed without refetching. Losing this file means re-spending
# credits to learn something we already know.
!data/serp-difficulty.json
!data/manual-pull/
data/manual-pull/*
!data/manual-pull/1-UPLOAD-THESE/
!data/manual-pull/2-DROP-RESULTS-HERE/
# Pulled Planner results are NOT churn. Each one costs a manual export that cannot be automated
# (no free Keyword Planner API), and the negation above re-includes only the DIRECTORY — the CSVs
# inside stayed untracked, so the first real pull sat unbacked-up until someone thought to ask.
# Track the files themselves.
!data/manual-pull/2-DROP-RESULTS-HERE/*.csv
!data/manual-pull/2-DROP-RESULTS-HERE/bd/
!data/manual-pull/2-DROP-RESULTS-HERE/bd/*.csv
